THE CODE AND THE DATA CARRY DIFFERENT LICENCES.

`LICENSE` (MIT) covers the source code in this repository, and only that.

It does not cover the images. Those are the work of third parties and remain
under their own terms — CC-BY, CC-BY-SA, CC0 and PDM, one licence per image.
This applies both to the sample committed under `data/output/sample_images/`
and to any dataset produced by running the pipeline.

Where to find the terms for a given image:

  data/output/manifest.json      per-image `license`, `license_url`,
                                 `attribution` and `source_url`
  data/output/dataset.csv        the same fields, in tabular form
  data/output/ATTRIBUTIONS.txt   ready-made credit lines, one per image

Retaining those credits is a condition of the CC-BY family and the reason
ATTRIBUTIONS.txt is generated on every run rather than written once by hand.

The pipeline only collects images whose licence permits both commercial use
and modification, and rejects any image whose licence it cannot determine —
see the licence policy in README.md. That is a deliberate constraint on what
this dataset contains; it is not legal advice about what you may do with it.
